WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.530
What would you think if Cristina Fernández
returned to control and dominate Argentina?

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:10.840
Could something like this even happen?

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:20.390
Dear viewers, last April 2019 a survey caused
a political earthquake in Argentina.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:25.830
An earthquake that also had significant economic
consequences.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:35.380
You see, the consultancy firm Isonomia, a
company that actually has close ties to the

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.460
government and has been working with Macri
for several years, noted that if the next

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.010
Argentinian elections reached the second round
– the first round will be held on October

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:49.320
27th and November 24th for the second round
– if that happened, Cristina Fernandez de

00:00:49.320 --> 00:01:01.640
Kirchner’s hypothetical candidacy would
win over the current president, Mauricio Macri.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:07.159
Right now, poor economic performance is causing
support for President Macri to plummet.

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:11.399
Inflation is extremely high, tariff increases
and the sense that nothing has really changed

00:01:11.399 --> 00:01:23.459
on a political level, has caused Mauricio
Macri’s popularity to drop like a rock.

00:01:23.459 --> 00:01:31.700
But just a second folks.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.079
On May 18th, a second political earthquake
shook Argentina.

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:38.960
For the first time in history, a vice presidential
candidate named her choice for president.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:45.450
You can not change a country only with a good
government, in its three branches of power.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:50.520
To change a country you need good government
and a good society.)

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.889
Cristina Fernandez made her decision to stand
for election public... but not as number one,

00:01:55.889 --> 00:01:59.569
as number two, as a vice presidential candidate.

00:01:59.569 --> 00:02:03.719
Former Argentine President Kirchner Seeks
Return to Power, as Vice President.

00:02:03.719 --> 00:02:04.719
New York Times)

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:05.719
You heard that correctly.

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:09.209
In the end, the Kirchnerist candidate will
be Alberto Fernández, Néstor Kirchner’s

00:02:09.209 --> 00:02:10.209
Chief of Staff.

00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:13.530
He also held that post in Cristina’s government
for one year.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.829
I’ve asked Alberto Fernandez to lead the
formula that we will run together, he as the

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:24.329
presidential candidate and I as vice-president,
to participate in the upcoming primary, open,

00:02:24.329 --> 00:02:26.659
simultaneous and mandatory elections”.

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:28.269
Cristina Fernández de Kirchner)

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:32.900
Folks, faced with this leadership scenario
at least three questions surface:

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.671
The first is easy; Why on earth did Kirchner
decide to do this?

00:02:35.671 --> 00:02:40.160
This takes time, effort, perseverance with
the objectives.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.189
Nobody can do things in two or three years)

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:48.739
Well... let's say that the answer has a lot
to do with her currently good popularity.

00:02:48.739 --> 00:02:53.200
As we’ve seen, for the first time since
2015, several polls placed Kirchner as the

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.969
winner for not only the first but also the
second round.

00:02:56.969 --> 00:03:05.329
And in the meantime address all friends, colleagues,
officials who have some dollars in fixed term

00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:06.329
deposits.

00:03:06.329 --> 00:03:07.650
You Moreno, right?)

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.939
Now, just a second.

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:12.890
The same forecasts also indicated a high number
of undecided votes.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:17.049
And, folks, this was very clear to election
experts: the fear of Kirchner’s return,

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:22.830
once it’s election time, could shift many
votes back to the current ruling party.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:28.950
However, with this decision, two things happen:
on the one hand, fear of the former president

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:32.290
is somewhat diluted; she’s no longer a presidential
candidate.

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:37.360
And on the other, the new duo could reach
voters that Kirchner alone would never have

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.360
reached.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:45.799
Allow me to explain: Alberto Fernandez’s
candidacy puts Regenerationism on the table,

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:50.260
his discourse is more moderate and there’s
the idea that the new duo would apply different

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.269
policies to those implemented by Cristina
in the past.

00:03:53.269 --> 00:03:56.029
Which is essential to achieve victory.

00:03:56.029 --> 00:03:59.439
Because of course, if you want to win the
elections, you can’t just count on your

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:00.439
stalwarts.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:07.579
you have to convince new voters while also
taking care not to mobilize your rival’s

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:10.650
vote.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:18.120
As Vice President, Cristina contributes all
her electoral strength without causing excessive

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.120
fear.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:22.450
So, based on this scenario, folks, the former
president’s decisions multiply her options

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.690
of returning to power.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:26.310
And that’s what she cares about the most.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:30.669
Not just because she likes power, but because
she needs to maintain the rights that go with

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:36.039
being a high level politician in order to
survive.

00:04:36.039 --> 00:04:40.250
Cristina Fernández de Kirchner needed to
participate in the elections due to a legal

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.060
situation, which we already discussed here
on VISUALPOLITIK.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:47.301
The ex-president has ten prosecutions and
five preventive detention requests.

00:04:47.301 --> 00:04:54.120
Folks, the only reason she isn’t already
in jail is because she still has her senator

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.120
privileges.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.599
The Senate, which is dominated by the Peronists,
has not withdrawn them.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:05.009
So, the first question, why did she decide
to run as Vice President? has been answered.

00:05:05.009 --> 00:05:08.060
The second question is, can this pairing really
win the elections?

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:16.530
I mean, Are we serious?! after the previous
government’s terrible results and all the

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.370
corruption?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:28.220
“They extend Cristina Kirchner’s processing
in notebook scandal,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:34.580
Judge Claudio Bonadio considered her a “co-author
of five other acts of bribery” and raised

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:37.520
the embargo against her to 80 million pesos.”

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.610
Profile)

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.780
Well… yeah.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:46.639
At least that’s what the voter intention
studies say.

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:47.639
Surveys such as those of Analía del Franco
or Ricardo Rouvier y Asociados placed Kirchner

00:05:47.639 --> 00:05:50.930
ahead with an advantage of 9.5 and 4 points
respectively.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:55.000
We can also find surveys, even more important
ones, which put Macri in the lead, but by

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.800
an increasingly smaller margin.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.099
And of course, now with the new formula many
of the fears of Kirchnerism have diluted,

00:06:01.099 --> 00:06:04.910
particularly because Alberto Fernández himself
was very critical of the former President:

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:06.320
“It’s hard to find something virtuous
in Cristina’s last mandate”.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:07.320
Alberto Fernández, 2015)

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.680
"She even said that Germany was worse than
us in terms of poverty, maintained that the

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:17.500
stocks didn’t exist and that inflation didn’t
matter to the end, that’s denial, a stubborn,

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.020
sometimes absurd denial" Alberto Fernández,
2015)

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.449
That is, how, overnight, the Kirchner-created
formula can be seen as a sign of change.

00:06:27.449 --> 00:06:28.449
Something like...

00:06:28.449 --> 00:06:32.280
“Hey, we learned from our mistakes, but
our intentions were always good, now we’ve

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:37.500
got it figured out and the important thing
isn’t a person’s job title but the project”.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.159
Incredible, huh?

00:06:39.159 --> 00:06:42.470
Now, let's be clear.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:48.940
you can’t really say that this is a surprising
or exceptional scenario, not at all.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.229
It’s part of a fairly predictable trend.

00:06:52.229 --> 00:06:56.889
Macri has gone from leading the polls in January
to drawing with Cristina in March and then

00:06:56.889 --> 00:07:03.060
to lagging behind her in April.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.879
As incredible as it may seem, according to
the polls, Christina’s support hasn’t

00:07:06.879 --> 00:07:07.879
stopped rising.

00:07:07.879 --> 00:07:11.620
The former president has gone from being a
headache to Peronism, which wanted to revamp

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:15.780
its image to becoming its best wild card,
a chance of recovering the government of the

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:18.150
republic.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:25.560
At the moment it seems like the evolution
of the economy will be the decisive factor.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:29.970
If things weren’t so bad, perhaps even Macri
could get enough support from the undecided

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:32.389
voters to remain in the Casa Rosada.

00:07:32.389 --> 00:07:33.389
The problem?

00:07:33.389 --> 00:07:37.750
As things stand, improving the economic situation
in the short term seems quite complicated.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:42.879
And that’s Kirchner’s best card right
now, one more slip and Macri is sent to the

00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:43.879
bench.

00:07:43.879 --> 00:07:50.190
You see, the Argentine economy is going through
a very, very fragile timet.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.729
Inflation in March was 4.7%.

00:07:51.729 --> 00:07:55.129
That’s the rate for one month, not one year.

00:07:55.129 --> 00:08:01.460
2019 could close with a 35 to 50% inflation
rate; the peso just keeps falling against

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:06.069
the dollar, stocks aren’t doing well either,
the country’s risk is now over 1000 points

00:08:06.069 --> 00:08:09.530
and the country is still in recession.

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:15.409
Folks, the race between Macri and Kirchner’s
hypothetical candidacies had become a race

00:08:15.409 --> 00:08:18.840
to be the least bad in the eyes of public
opinion.

00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:30.189
And no, this is not a criticism, it’s simply
fact:

00:08:30.189 --> 00:08:35.220
Both Cristina Fernández de Kirchner and Mauricio
Macri are reaping very negative evaluations

00:08:35.220 --> 00:08:36.610
from the Argentinians.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:40.750
In the case of the current president, according
to surveys, up to 84% of Argentinians have

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.330
a negative opinion of him.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:46.600
On the other hand, though it may seem incredible
given all the scandals, the former president’s

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:49.880
data are somewhat better, but not that much.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.920
In her case, the negative opinion score is
76%

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:59.130
But now with the arrival of Alberto Fernández
things are different.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:01.940
The new candidate is less "tainted" than the
former president.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:07.930
I mean, I don’t think that instead of going
back five years with president Cristina, we

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:13.180
go back fifteen to something similar to Néstor,
lowering Cristina and raising Alberto Fernández

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:16.630
means a substantial change for the economy
or for people's lives.

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:17.630
I don’t think so.)

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:21.631
So, the third and most important question
based on what we’ve seen would be: What

00:09:21.631 --> 00:09:25.350
consequences would the victory of Alberto
Fernández and Cristina Fernández de Kirchner

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.200
have and on what kind of public policies would
they bet?

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:36.540
Well, it turns out we don’t even have to
wait until October to start answering.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:40.700
You see, the mere fact that Kirchner became
a favorite in the polls has already made all

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.280
international investors very, very nervous.

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:47.640
Well, perhaps it’s better to say, even more
nervous than they already were.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.710
And that has translated into a new drop of
the peso against the dollar.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:58.050
Which may have also fueled the idea of ​​this
new and surprising formula.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.570
Now, why so much nervousness?

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:05.190
Because it was assumed that Cristina’s return
to power would mean a return to the same ultra-interventionist

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:09.010
policies and tons of public spending, as in
the previous stage.

00:10:09.010 --> 00:10:13.370
Ok, Macri didn’t lead to any great change
either, but if Cristina returned, any possibility

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:17.900
of Argentina changing – and don’t tell
me it doesn’t need a change – would go

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:18.900
out the window.

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:26.950
The simple fact that Kirchner took the lead
in the polls fueled investors' fear of a new

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:28.760
and upcoming Argentine default.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:32.770
And, folks, that makes things even worse...
to such an extent that even some analysts,

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:37.850
such as Carlos Malamud, have warned of a forthcoming
exchange run – that is, the peso will sink

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:43.220
even more because everyone will want to get
rid of that currency – if Kirchnerism continues

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:47.470
to improve its chances of getting back in
power.

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:54.201
In any case, regardless of whether Macri wins
or loses the elections, Argentina’s current

00:10:54.201 --> 00:10:56.080
situation is complicated.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:01.360
The government will have to return a whopping
34 billion dollars in 2020, in a context of

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:06.830
severe economic recession and with a peso
that is depreciating at full speed.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:11.470
Argentina is at a crossroads: its debt in
dollars is huge, accounting for almost 90%

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:15.390
of the GDP, a figure that won’t stop increasing
due to the peso’s collapse.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:19.870
The more the peso falls, the greater the burden
of the debt in dollars for the Argentine economy.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:23.870
The probability that Argentina will not succeed
in paying this debt within one presidential

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.750
term is high.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:32.770
Yes, the probability of default is high, but
it isn’t a fact.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:37.040
The situation is not yet irreversible and
fortunately it seems that almost all political

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.430
leaders are clear on this.

00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.940
The fact that Cristina has decided to run
as Vice President in Alberto Fernández’s

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.530
candidacy could be a good test.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:49.660
After all, as we’ve already seen, Alberto
Fernández was very critical of Cristina Fernández’s

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.380
management.

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:53.110
However...

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:55.710
Argentina does need a total change of course.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:12:00.360
And, to be frank, Alberto Fernández doesn’t
seem so committed to leading that change given

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.760
his current running mate is the former president.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:03.760
Don’t you think?

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:07.250
And folks, that is what leads us directly
to this video’s main question:

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:12.070
Will the new government, be it Macri, Fernandez
or any other candidate, be willing to carry

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:13.920
out that massive change?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.320
Leave your answer in the comments as well
as in the survey.

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:20.600
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:21.890
subscribe for brand new videos.

